## Naming Conventions

- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/hero-section)
- Use PascalCase for component files (e.g., HeroSection.astro)
- Use camelCase for utility files (e.g., formatDate.ts)
- Use kebab-case for content collection slugs and URLs
- Follow action-object pattern for utilities (e.g., parse-markdown.ts)
- Use semantic naming for design tokens (primary, secondary, etc.)

## TypeScript Usage

- Use TypeScript strict mode (required in tsconfig.json)
- Prefer interfaces over types for component props
- Avoid enums; use const objects with 'as const' assertion
- Define strict types for Content Collections schemas
- Use Astro.props typing for component props
- **NEW**: When wrapping Astro components, use pragmatic TypeScript patterns:
  - Prefer `ComponentProps<typeof Component>` for extending framework components
  - Use `@ts-ignore` with clear comments for complex framework type intersections
  - Document reasoning in ADRs when using type escape hatches
- Implement absolute imports with @ aliases:

```typescript
  "@/*": ["src/*"]
  "@components/*": ["src/components/*"]
  "@layouts/*": ["src/layouts/*"]
  "@utils/*": ["src/utils/*"]
  "@styles/*": ["src/styles/*"]
  "@types/*": ["src/types/*"]
  "@content/*": ["src/content/*"]
  ```

## Astro-Specific Patterns

- Use zero JavaScript by default; add interactivity strategically
- Follow progressive enhancement: CSS → View Transitions → Alpine.js → Preact islands
- Use proper client directives:
  - `client:visible` (lazy load when in viewport)
  - `client:idle` (load when browser idle)
  - `client:media` (responsive loading)
  - `client:only` (skip SSR - rare use)
  - **Never**: `client:load` unless justified in ADR
- Implement Content Collections for all structured content with type-safe schemas
- Use Astro components for static content, framework components only for complex state

## Design System Implementation

- Use design tokens as single source of truth in `tokens/` directory
- Build tokens to CSS variables and Tailwind config via `pnpm run build:tokens`
- Token structure: `tokens/base.json` → `tokens/dist/tokens.css` + Tailwind integration
- Implement dark mode with system preference detection using `.dark` class
- Follow WCAG AA accessibility standards with automated contrast validation
- Use semantic color naming (background, foreground, primary, secondary, etc.)
- Include motion tokens for consistent animations and transitions

## Starlight Documentation Rules

- All documentation lives under src/content/docs/
- Always include a front-matter title, description, lastUpdated, tableOfContents, pagefind
- Keep the page’s first written heading at h2 or lower
- Link to other docs pages with clean slugs—no file extensions
- Configure sidebar navigation via starlight.sidebar
- Write call-outs with triple-colon asides
- Fence code blocks and lean on Expressive Code
- Start links with / or use a root-relative path—never hard-code the site’s base prefix

## Performance Requirements

- Target Lighthouse scores: Performance 100, Accessibility 100, Best Practices 100, SEO 100
- Implement performance budgets with CI enforcement via Lighthouse CI
- Use Astro's built-in image optimization (no external CDNs)
- Minimize bundle size through zero-JS default and strategic islands
- Implement proper caching strategies with `public/_headers`
- Monitor Core Web Vitals: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1

